;
; Primer Dark for Kvantum.
; Colors are derived from GitHub Primer Primitives (MIT) and match
; kde/colors/PrimerDark.colors so Qt applications styled by Breeze and by
; Kvantum resolve the same semantic roles.
;
; This theme defines the documented GeneralColors color spec and the theme
; metadata only. Kvantum reads any key that is absent from the built-in
; default configuration, so the artwork, geometry, and behavior keys stay at
; their Kvantum defaults. Kvantum paints its widgets from an SVG image and
; falls back per element to its built-in default SVG, so this theme colors the
; style without replacing that artwork.

[%General]
author=Reda Salmi
comment=An unofficial Primer Dark theme for Kvantum

[GeneralColors]
window.color=#010409
inactive.window.color=#0D1117
base.color=#0D1117
inactive.base.color=#0D1117
alt.base.color=#151B23
inactive.alt.base.color=#151B23
button.color=#212830
light.color=#262C36
mid.light.color=#3D444D
dark.color=#010409
mid.color=#2F3742
shadow.color=#010409
highlight.color=#1F6FEB
inactive.highlight.color=#1F6FEB
tooltip.base.color=#212830
text.color=#F0F6FC
inactive.text.color=#F0F6FC
window.text.color=#F0F6FC
inactive.window.text.color=#9198A1
button.text.color=#F0F6FC
disabled.text.color=#656C76
tooltip.text.color=#F0F6FC
highlight.text.color=#FFFFFF
inactive.highlight.text.color=#FFFFFF
link.color=#4493F8
link.visited.color=#AB7DF8
progress.indicator.text.color=#FFFFFF
progress.inactive.indicator.text.color=#F0F6FC
